    {
      "id": "f7b279177941f6da610cfb983cf75fafd5669ab2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 475881755,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't think that's correct in general:\n\n- if the commits are not related, they will be melted\n- the commit message is taken from MR title. That can be not meaningful enough. What I'm doing for instance, is working on remove compiler warnings, re-using a merge request titled \"Compiler warnings\". Every commit contains a change for a single dissector, that looks better to me.\n\nSo, I would never squash commits into one. When the author pushes a messed MR, request the author to squash themselves. See !1524: if the commits will get squashed, a commit with the very same commit message as this one will pop up in master, getting harder to understand what they contain.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-30T13:35:37.515Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-30T13:35:37.515Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 83226811,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1522,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f9fe214cb303d04fd8ebb20b0813483acd912c19",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 475892065,
          "type": null,
          "body": "That puts a lot on the reviewer IMHO. With gerrit we gad a different workflow, one MR one issue.\nThis makes reviewing less apealing...",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-30T13:44:55.512Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-30T13:44:55.512Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 83226811,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1522,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a73a0400c08351b606471d5879494ce08010ec4b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 475897831,
          "type": null,
          "body": "If we want to stick with that model, that must be enforced and explained. People using fork/MR workflow on gitlab and github don't expect their commit to be changed. A MR is expected by definition to contain more than one commit.\n\nConsider a MR with:\n\n- one important bug fix\n- one giant indentation fix\n- one meaningless commit message by squash like \"some work\"\n\nFor some reason the indentation fix is messy and another one reverts it to start over. In the mess, the important fix gets lost. Moreover the ownership of the commit must be preserved (to be honest I don't get why gitlab allow a merger to squash commits).",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-30T13:51:39.527Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-30T13:51:39.527Z",
